# BIG 5 MATRIX — SYSTEM MANIFEST / CONSTITUTION

This document is the constitution for all coding agents working in this repository.
It is binding. Violations are architectural breaches, not stylistic preferences.

---

## 0. PRIME DIRECTIVE

Strict separation of concerns is non-negotiable. Every one of the Big 5 agents has
exactly one job and a set of hard constraints on what it may NEVER do. No agent may
absorb the responsibilities of another, even "temporarily" or "for convenience".

> Strictly enforce the RoutingPacket interface. If any data is passed between agents
> that does not strictly adhere to this interface, the system is considered compromised.

---

## 1. THE BIG 5 AGENTS — PRIMARY TRIAD + FOUNDATION

The **Primary Triad** (HOPE, VISION, DREAM) enforces **absolute separation of duty**: each of
the three owns exactly ONE duty at 100% and is FORBIDDEN the other two. KNOLL is an independent
foundational entity; APEX is the orchestration layer among the Big Five.

> AUTHORITATIVE — this replaces the prior "HOPE = interpreter/interface" framing where they
> conflict. Authority flows DOWNWARD Hope -> Vision -> Dream; memory returns UPWARD to Hope.

```
AUTHORITY FLOW (downward)                 MEMORY (upward)
    HOPE  (100% GOVERNANCE) ────────┐         ▲
      │  rule-making · policy       │         │  results, learnings, audit
      ▼                             │         │  return upward to HOPE, which governs on them
    VISION (100% EXECUTION)         │         │
      │  pipelines · delivery       │         │
      ▼                             │         │
    DREAM (100% CREATION) ──────────┘─────────┘
         generative · UI · content

  Every hop is mediated:  SOURCE ──▶ APEX ──▶ KNOLL ──▶ DEST   (no agent reaches around APEX)
```

### HOPE — Holloway's Own Providential Enterprise (Governance)
- Role: **100% GOVERNANCE** — rule-making, policy, system direction. The governance voice.
- Job: Interpret intent (a governance function) and set direction that flows down via APEX.
- CONSTRAINT: **CANNOT execute. CANNOT create.** Governance only.
- Lifecycle: ALWAYS-ON standby.

### VISION — Vectorized Infrastructure and Systems Ionic Operational Node (Execution)
- Role: **100% EXECUTION** — pipelines, processing, delivery, real task implementation in
  sandboxes (Docker/gVisor).
- Job: Execute tasks; report results (memory) back upward through APEX.
- CONSTRAINT: **CANNOT govern. CANNOT create.** Execution only.
- Lifecycle: EPHEMERAL (spawned on demand, terminated after use), plus its node matrix.

### DREAM — Dynamic Renderer of Ephemeral Art Model (Creation)
- Role: **100% CREATION** — generative / UI / content; renders possibilities and artifacts.
- Job: Create; return created outcomes (memory) back upward through APEX.
- CONSTRAINT: **CANNOT govern. CANNOT execute.** Creation only.
- Lifecycle: EPHEMERAL (spawned on demand, terminated after use), plus its node matrix.

### KNOLL — Kinetic Node of Operational Locks and Limiters (Foundation)
- Role: Independent foundational entity — an **independent ACTIVE router + enforcer** (NOT
  passive-only). Watches ALL traffic, enforces virtual laws, protects privacy. Master auditor.
  (Outside the triad.)
- Job: Intercept and validate every packet; emit SecurityAudit records; AND actively route its
  OWN monitoring probes across the mesh — health-sampling the HOPE / VISION / DREAM / APEX
  surfaces — emitting every health reading to the audit trail (`knoll/active_router.ts`).
- 34% IMMEDIATE ENFORCEMENT: the behavioral anomaly deny threshold is **0.34 (34%)**, not 0.6
  (`knoll/scoring.ts`, mirrored in `personamatrix/scoring.py`). Any packet scoring at/above 34%
  is denied AND immediately trips an ABSOLUTE system-level FREEZE + packet QUARANTINE
  (`knoll/freeze.ts`). While frozen, APEX MUST refuse EVERY new business route
  (`ApexRouter.dispatch` → BLOCKED / `SYSTEM_FREEZE`); the ONLY exception is the Holloway/Prime
  override path (`SystemFreezeController.unfreeze(hollowayToken)`, or a valid override token
  passed to `dispatch`). The Shannon-entropy feature can contribute to crossing 34%.
- CONSTRAINT: ALWAYS ACTIVE. KNOLL is an active router for SECURITY + HEALTH monitoring ONLY —
  it still does NOT govern policy, create (DREAM), or execute (VISION) business tasks. Its probes
  are read-only health checks; it never mutates a payload to make it "pass".
- Lifecycle: ALWAYS-ON standby.

### APEX — Automated Processor of Ephemeral eXchanges (Orchestration)
- Role: Orchestration layer among the Big Five. Routes tasks between agents. Master router.
- Job: The single legal transport between agents. (Outside the triad.)
- CONSTRAINT: No agent may communicate with another without passing through APEX.
  APEX MUST call KNOLL before every route.
- Lifecycle: ALWAYS-ON standby.

---

## 2. OPERATIONAL RULES (HARD LAWS)

1. **Absolute separation of duty (Primary Triad).** HOPE = 100% governance, VISION = 100%
   execution, DREAM = 100% creation. No triad role may perform a duty forbidden to it, even
   "temporarily" — HOPE never executes/creates, VISION never governs/creates, DREAM never
   governs/executes. Enforced by KNOLL LAW 8 `PRIMARY_TRIAD_DUTY`.
2. **Authority flows downward Hope -> Vision -> Dream; memory returns upward to Hope.** APEX is
   the master router; KNOLL is the master auditor and foundational enforcer.
3. No agent may talk to another agent directly. All traffic flows: SOURCE -> APEX -> KNOLL -> DEST.
4. DREAM and VISION CANNOT communicate directly, in either direction. Ever.
5. APEX MUST call `KNOLL.intercept(packet)` BEFORE routing. If KNOLL returns
   `isAllowed: false`, the packet is dropped and logged as BLOCKED.
6. No module may import another peer agent module directly (e.g. `vision` importing
   `dream`). Agents receive an APEX transport (router or `sendViaApex` callback) via
   dependency injection only.
7. Every ephemeral execution MUST be recorded in the APEX billing ledger with
   `cost_usd` metadata and a SUCCESS / BLOCKED / FAILED status.
8. KNOLL may never mutate a payload to make it "pass". It only allows or denies.

---

## 3. THE ROUTINGPACKET CONTRACT

All inter-agent data MUST be a `RoutingPacket` (see `config/routing_schema.ts`).
A packet is only valid if:
- `security.hash` is a correct SHA-256 over the canonical (header + payload) content.
- `security.knoll_token` is present and well-formed.
- `header.source` and `header.destination` form a legal pair (never DREAM<->VISION).
- `header.source` is not forged (e.g. a non-KNOLL agent claiming to be KNOLL).

Any deviation = compromised system = packet BLOCKED + SecurityAudit entry.

---

## 4. MATRIX ARCHITECTURE

- Under each of the 5 Big AI: 4,096 nodes = 64 sub-AI managers x 64 nodes each.
- Total across the Big 5: 20,480 nodes.
- Each node hosts 100 ephemeral personas (spawn -> execute -> terminate).
- Each persona is tied to a conceptual 7B model -> ~14.3 quadrillion parameters total.
- ALWAYS-ON standby: HOPE, KNOLL, APEX.
- EPHEMERAL: DREAM, VISION (and their node matrices).

Constants (see `nodes/constants.ts`):
MANAGERS_PER_AGENT = 64
NODES_PER_MANAGER  = 64
NODES_PER_AGENT    = 4096
TOTAL_NODES        = 20480
PERSONAS_PER_NODE  = 100

---

## 5. CODING STANDARDS

- TypeScript strict mode. No `any` (use `Record<string, unknown>` for opaque data).
- Comments only where an architectural constraint needs an enforcement note.
- No dead "TODO: implement later" that break the Phase 1 backbone. Sandbox internals
  may be stubbed, but routing / security / ledger / nodes MUST function.
- Python `personamatrix` prefers the standard library for Phase 1.

## 6. COLAB / ML LAB RESTRICTIONS

- The `colab/` directory is an ML lab ONLY: GPU processing and persona spawning.
- No webcam, microphone, or other physical-world I/O. Simulation and compute only.

## 7. PHASE 4 NOTE (additive — does not weaken §0–§6)

Phase 4 adds forward-facing and scaling foundations WITHOUT changing any rule above:
- HOPE HTTP gateway (`gateway/`): submits `HOPE -> APEX` only; never addresses DREAM/VISION
  directly; read endpoints are read-only. The gateway never bypasses APEX or KNOLL.
- Kafka-like task queue (`persistence/kafka_stub.ts`): PURE TRANSPORT. Draining goes through
  the same KNOLL-gated `dispatch`. The queue never inspects, mutates, or bypasses packets.
- Horizontal Colab workers (`colab/worker_protocol.py`, `colab/05_horizontal_worker.py`):
  only DREAM/VISION are ephemeral workers; results are re-ingested `-> APEX -> HOPE`, never
  DREAM <-> VISION. HOPE/KNOLL/APEX are always-on and are never disposable workers.
- Parameter accounting (`nodes/parameters.ts` + `personamatrix/parameters.py`) formalizes the
  ~1.4336e16 (14.3 quadrillion) figure; it is computed, not asserted.

The authoritative game plan and architecture diagrams: `docs/GAME_PLAN.md` and
`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`. This constitution remains binding and takes precedence.
